{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity","id":1421561,"title":"[\u00c6on] Nova's on Earth in Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-02T22:42:33-08:00","id":1421561,"title":"[\u00c6on] Nova's on Earth in Trinity","content":"Here's a question since I haven't seen anything rules related to novas in Trinity.<br /> <br /> Is earth so contaminated by Flux that there's no way for a newly erupted Nova to stay sane? Because so far, all the Novas, outside of the Japanese Novas, seem to be either crazy or heading that way.<br /> <br /> So is it something that has changed on teh planet, or just the effect of &quot;everyone is trying to kill me, and I must remain hidden or become strong enough to fight&quot; neither one of which is really conducive to sanity.<br /> <br /> In 1E, supposedly Nippon had a treatment to make &quot;Sane&quot; novas, but that has been superseded by the Superior Treatment--and the only thing mentioned about their own Novas' was that they had a series of tests that could determine if they might fall to taint. <br /> <br /> But the tests weren't defined, so It's unknown if they were physical or mental in nature, IE is Mr. Nova naturally resistant to taint or is his <i>personality</i> resistant to the kinds of actions ond overreach that led to corruption. <br /> <br /> <br /> But that gets back to the ultimate question--is it possible to erupt and stay sane as a Nova on earth. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T23:45:40-08:00","id":1421566,"title":"","content":"You have to ask the backers of the Aberrant PDF if hard rules are in there regarding that.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the setting implies - that overusage of Quantum and expanding the powers quickly accelerates the syndrome. I\u00b4d also reckon that circumstance will have an effect on a new aberrant. Activated by another Mutant or ina Zone? or a more natural eruption and a slower learning process. But as there is no &quot;School for gifted Novas&quot;, Aberrants a quite alone in this and thus a prone to get lost to Quantum mutations. So you have multiple factors: Eruption intensity, circumstances, personality, mental stability, convictions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T00:27:18-08:00","id":1421568,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s more a narrative thing. Earth of the Aeon era doesn\u2019t have any/many \u2018clean\u2019 Quantum Flux areas for \u2018novas\u2019 to erupt. It\u2019s flush with psi energies that interfere with Quantum, and the Quantum areas are twisted into being more damaging Corruption. So when people experience the rare Quantum eruptions in the Aeon era, they\u2019re more likely to rapidly suffer physical and mental transformations that mark them as monsters to the rest of humanity. <br /> <br /> Aberrants are bad guys in the Aeon era. There\u2019s nothing stopping you from having sane novas erupt in that era in your game, but the prime timeline is going to assume this doesn\u2019t happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T06:02:39-08:00","id":1421604,"title":"","content":"My approach is Novas aren\u2019t completely natural, as they require a high level of \u201cquantum background field\u201d to erupt. If the quantum is \u201cclean\u201d the eruption is less likely to create a Aberrant and more prone to create a Nova.<br /> <br /> During Nova era Mal\u2019s device created the initial kick to let the first novas to erupt and their presence and powers erupted others in the following years. As more Novas went corrupted the background field become more and more corrupted and more prone to create Aberrants instead of Novas.<br /> <br /> The Ultimatum reduced the general Quantum level, reducing the chances of a Nova or Aberrant to Erupt and Burano made it weaker and less corrupted, later with Psions going around everywhere the quantum background is reduced even more.<br /> <br /> So the chances of a Nova to erupt randomly is extremely close to 0, while Aberrants will probably erupt once in a while in a QFZ (most people will be sub Aberrants, but maybe 1 in 10 million will be a regular Aberrant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T07:30:23-08:00","id":1421619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity#post1421561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question since I haven't seen anything rules related to novas in Trinity.<br /> <br /> Is earth so contaminated by Flux that there's no way for a newly erupted Nova to stay sane? Because so far, all the Novas, outside of the Japanese Novas, seem to be either crazy or heading that way.<br /> <br /> So is it something that has changed on teh planet, or just the effect of &amp;quot;everyone is trying to kill me, and I must remain hidden or become strong enough to fight&amp;quot; neither one of which is really conducive to sanity.<br /> <br /> In 1E, supposedly Nippon had a treatment to make &amp;quot;Sane&amp;quot; novas, but that has been superseded by the Superior Treatment--and the only thing mentioned about their own Novas' was that they had a series of tests that could determine if they might fall to taint. <br /> <br /> But the tests weren't defined, so It's unknown if they were physical or mental in nature, IE is Mr. Nova naturally resistant to taint or is his <i>personality</i> resistant to the kinds of actions ond overreach that led to corruption. <br /> <br /> <br /> But that gets back to the ultimate question--is it possible to erupt and stay sane as a Nova on earth. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good question. Overall I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:14:50-08:00","id":1421631,"title":"","content":"Now the other side of the coin: Sub Aberrants during Nova Age.<br /> <br /> A Nova can create a sub aberrant by healing a person too much during a single day, stacking flux until the person gather 4+ Transcendence. I would say the person develop a \u201cquantum induced Cancer\u201d, that would be called Quantum Disease latter in Aeon.<br /> By regular rules, a high transcendence human would have transformations, but power need to be house ruled, I probably would give quantum 1 (not possible to raise, but still being a Tier 2 character), allow body modifications and some Mega Edges that can be bought with Q1 and no Mega Attributes.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T09:18:32-08:00","id":1421633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity?p=1421631#post1421631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the other side of the coin: Sub Aberrants during Nova Age.<br /> <br /> A Nova can create a sub aberrant by healing a person too much during a single day, stacking flux until the person gather 4+ Transcendence. I would say the person develop a \u201cquantum induced Cancer\u201d, that would be called Quantum Disease latter in Aeon.<br /> By regular rules, a high transcendence human would have transformations, but power need to be house ruled, I probably would give quantum 1 (not possible to raise, but still being a Tier 2 character), allow body modifications and some Mega Edges that can be bought with Q1 and no Mega Attributes.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like your idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T11:45:03-08:00","id":1421657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity?p=1421631#post1421631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the other side of the coin: Sub Aberrants during Nova Age.<br /> <br /> A Nova can create a sub aberrant by healing a person too much during a single day, stacking flux until the person gather 4+ Transcendence. I would say the person develop a \u201cquantum induced Cancer\u201d, that would be called Quantum Disease latter in Aeon.<br /> By regular rules, a high transcendence human would have transformations, but power need to be house ruled, I probably would give quantum 1 (not possible to raise, but still being a Tier 2 character), allow body modifications and some Mega Edges that can be bought with Q1 and no Mega Attributes.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been tinkering with a post apocalyptic setting, and I definitely want Sub-Aberrant Mutants (just \u201cMutants\u201d in that setting) to be a playable Tier 2 characters. Sort of anti-Superiors, reflecting aspects of Novas that Superiors don\u2019t, and not the enhanced attributes part of the equation that they do.<br /> <br /> So yeah, similar page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:03:12-08:00","id":1421666,"title":"","content":"In this case I would go for powers limited to Q1 and 2.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I have in my mind Q1-2 is T2, Q3-5 T3, Q6+ T4. It would make the Nova/Psiad/Talent crossover a bit smoother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:34:40-08:00","id":1421672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity?p=1421631#post1421631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the other side of the coin: Sub Aberrants during Nova Age.<br /> <br /> A Nova can create a sub aberrant by healing a person too much during a single day, stacking flux until the person gather 4+ Transcendence. I would say the person develop a \u201cquantum induced Cancer\u201d, that would be called Quantum Disease latter in Aeon.<br /> By regular rules, a high transcendence human would have transformations, but power need to be house ruled, I probably would give quantum 1 (not possible to raise, but still being a Tier 2 character), allow body modifications and some Mega Edges that can be bought with Q1 and no Mega Attributes.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use the rules to create an agent as a guide to create Sub Aberrants. And have some comparison on when to give a dot of power or Mega attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T07:11:52-07:00","id":1453645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity?p=1421666#post1421666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case I would go for powers limited to Q1 and 2.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I have in my mind Q1-2 is T2, Q3-5 T3, Q6+ T4. It would make the Nova/Psiad/Talent crossover a bit smoother.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many points would they start with? I was thinking 30ish. With max Q 2 at creation. And Q4 as a ceiling before corruption consumes them. And I agree, tier 3 at Q3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T09:54:09-07:00","id":1453656,"title":"","content":"Try this idea. A Nova, who thought she'd return to Earth in a few years, built a device that nondestructively inhibited Nova erruption. And she hid this device in her family's upstate NY estate. The device had a one hundred-fifty mile radius (the maker thought her gizmo might have a three mile radius tops). An unforseen side effect of the device creates a subtle aura around people with high potential to errupt. This aura is off-putting to baseline humans but attractive to potential Novas. <br /> <br /> Thus in the Aeon period, there are people in the effect radius of this device who were born with Node Brains. One of the Ghost of Cincinnatus comunities is within this radius.<br /> <br /> When the device finally burns out, several Novas with high levels of Taint resistance errupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T16:27:44-07:00","id":1453673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421561-\u00e6on-nova-s-on-earth-in-trinity?p=1453645#post1453645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many points would they start with? I was thinking 30ish. With max Q 2 at creation. And Q4 as a ceiling before corruption consumes them. And I agree, tier 3 at Q3.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s hard to say a fixed number because it changes with the other characters working. A single Nova in a group of Psiads may be weaker because they can help each other (not as much as Psions, but still), while a group of novas with a single Psiad would put the Psiad in a bad situation. But something between 60 and 75 XP would make them even in a general way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}